# Reference Section Content

Grammar reference for understanding how Greek works: cases, articles, nouns, pronouns, adjectives, prepositions, verbs and patterns. Public: no auth guard.

## Route Structure

```
/reference                    Landing page (SectionIndex)
/reference/:tab               $tab.tsx: cases, articles, nouns, pronouns, adjectives, prepositions, patterns
/reference/verbs              verbs/route.tsx layout (own route family, not a :tab)
/reference/verbs/             redirects to /reference/verbs/present
/reference/verbs/:band        present, past, past-continuous, future
```

`$tab.tsx` checks `VALID_TABS`; any other `:tab` throws `notFound()` (404). Its `head` sets the document title with `pageTitle()` (`@/lib/page-title`) from the tab's `REFERENCE_TABS` label, e.g. "Cases · Kalimera". The verbs routes and the landing page set no title of their own. Unknown verb bands also throw `notFound()`.

Every tab page renders `ReferenceNav` (a `NavTabs` bar over `REFERENCE_TABS`) above its content.

## Landing Page

<route path="/reference">
<purpose>Section hub: a Greek-first table of contents for the grammar topics</purpose>
<file>src/routes/reference/index.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Shared `SectionIndex` (`src/components/SectionIndex.tsx`): title "Reference", lede "Grammar patterns and paradigms"
- Ruled rows, each led by the Greek name, then the English label and description. No cards, icons or tints.
  - The case system:
    - Πτώσεις / Cases: "What each ending is for"
    - Αντωνυμίες / Pronouns: "Cases in the words you use most"
  - Words that agree:
    - Άρθρα / Articles: "The definite article, case by case"
    - Ουσιαστικά / Nouns: "Endings by gender"
    - Επίθετα / Adjectives: "The noun's grammar, copied"
  - Building sentences:
    - Προθέσεις / Prepositions: "Little words, big relationships"
    - Ρήματα / Verbs: "Three patterns, thousands of verbs"
    - Δομές / Patterns: "Constructions that don't translate"
- Each row links to /reference/{section}
</displays>
</route>

## Tabs

`REFERENCE_TABS` in `components/reference-nav.tsx`, in nav order:

```
cases        → What each case is for (Doer / Target / Owner)
articles     → When to use the article, and every form it takes
nouns        → Noun endings by gender and case
pronouns     → Pronoun paradigms, placement and decision guide
adjectives   → Adjective agreement patterns
prepositions → Preposition + case combinations, σε contraction
verbs        → Conjugation by band (/reference/verbs/$band)
patterns     → Greek-specific constructions
```

## Data Source

Static content from constants:
- `@/constants/recognition` - CASE_ROLES, CASE_TRIGGERS
- `@/constants/agreement` - ARTICLE_AGREEMENT_QUICK_REF, AGREEMENT_PARADIGMS
- `@/constants/homographs` - HOMOGRAPH_ROWS (article or pronoun?)
- `@/constants/pronouns` - pronoun paradigms, examples, phrases
- `@/constants/adjectives` - adjective paradigms, examples, mistakes
- `@/constants/prepositions` - preposition data
- `@/constants/verbs` - verb patterns, aorist and future tables
- `@/constants/grammar-palette` - SCHEME, CASE_SCHEME, GENDER_SCHEME (colour)

Database, loaded in `$tab.tsx` only for the tab that needs it:
- `loadPatterns` (patterns): `getVocabBySlug` for the phrases and verbs sections, grouped by tag with `groupVocabByTag`
- `loadNouns` (nouns): `getNounsForParadigmReference`, grouped by `groupNounsByPattern`

Every page title is a `ReferenceHero` (title + thesis, optional `demo`). It has no eyebrow. Band headings are `BandHeading` (title + optional lede, no kicker); hand-offs are `NextStepCard` (title + description, optional `emphasis`, no kicker).

Practice CTAs are `PracticeCTA` with a `topic`; `drillHrefForTopic` in `src/lib/practice-links.ts` maps it. Logged-out visitors always go to /register; topics without a drill fall back to /practice.

