## Tab: cases

<tab route="/reference/cases">
<purpose>What each case is for: the three roles a word can play</purpose>
<file>src/routes/reference/tabs/cases.tsx</file>
<components>
- CasesSection (components/cases-section.tsx)
- ArticleParadigm (components/case-table.tsx)
</components>
<displays>
- Hero: "One word, many roles."
- Three TeachingCards (Doer / Target / Owner, grammar term as badge), each with a MarkedGreek example: only the marked words carry the case colour
- Ruled notes list: flexible word order, start with Doer and Target, everyday prepositions pull Target, both sides of είναι are Doer
- "Look it up" band: the shared ArticleParadigm, then "Trigger words that pull a case" as LookupCards (chip "Target triggers" / "Owner triggers", eyebrow = case name)
- "Picked the case. Now what?": NextStepCards to Articles (emphasis), Pronouns, Nouns
- No PracticeCTA
</displays>
<note>
Cases explain the SYSTEM, the other tabs show it in ACTION. See tabs/cases.content.llm.
</note>
</tab>

